    <!-- Security Model -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Security Model</h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 mb-4">
        Credential forwarding is designed for <strong>local development only</strong>. It uses multiple layers of security to protect your Azure credentials.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">mTLS Transport Security</h3>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
        <table class="min-w-full text-sm rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-neutral-200 dark:bg-neutral-700">
              <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Property</th>
              <th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Value</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800">
            <tr class="border-t border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">Key algorithm</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">ECDSA P-256</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">TLS version</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">TLS 1.3 (minimum)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">Certificate validity</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">24 hours (ephemeral)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">Client authentication</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">Required (mutual TLS)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700">
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">CA scope</td>
              <td class="py-3 px-4 text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">Per-session, ephemeral, never persisted to system trust store</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Additional Protections</h3>
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <div class="p-4 bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700">
          <div class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">Rate Limiting</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
            30 requests per minute per client IP. Prevents credential abuse even if the mTLS cert is compromised.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700">
          <div class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">Scope Validation</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
            Only HTTPS URLs are accepted as token scopes. Input is validated for printable ASCII characters with shell injection protection.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700">
          <div class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">Server Binding</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
            The auth server binds to <code class="px-1 bg-neutral-200 dark:bg-neutral-700 rounded">127.0.0.1</code> on Windows and macOS (only reachable from the host). On Linux, the bind address is configurable to support Docker's networking model.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700">
          <div class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">Certificate Cleanup</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
            All ephemeral certificates are cleaned up when <code class="px-1 bg-neutral-200 dark:bg-neutral-700 rounded">azd app run</code> stops. They are never written to the system trust store.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 rounded-lg border border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-700">
          <div class="font-semibold text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100 mb-1">Opt-in Model</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400">
            Credentials are <strong>never</strong> forwarded unless the developer explicitly sets <code class="px-1 bg-neutral-200 dark:bg-neutral-700 rounded">local.credentials: azd</code> on a service.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 p-6 bg-yellow-100 dark:bg-yellow-900/40 rounded-lg border border-yellow-300 dark:border-yellow-700">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2 text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">⚠️ Trust Boundary</h3>
        <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
          All containers with <code class="px-2 py-1 bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 rounded">local.credentials: azd</code> share the same trust boundary — they receive the same client certificate and can request tokens for any scope your Azure identity has access to. Only enable credential forwarding on containers you trust.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Troubleshooting -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Troubleshooting</h2>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">"azd auth token failed" inside the container</h3>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 mb-4">
        The most common cause is that you're not authenticated on the host. Run these commands on your <strong>host machine</strong> (not inside the container):
      </p>
      <Code code={troubleshootAuth} lang="bash" frame="terminal" />

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Container can't reach the host auth server</h3>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 mb-4">
        Verify the container can reach the host network:
      </p>
      <Code code={troubleshootNetwork} lang="bash" frame="terminal" />

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Permission denied on certificates</h3>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 mb-4">
        Verify the certificate volume mount is accessible:
      </p>
      <Code code={troubleshootPermissions} lang="bash" frame="terminal" />

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Rate limited (429 errors)</h3>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 mb-4">
        The auth server limits each client to 30 requests per minute. If you're hitting this limit:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300 space-y-2">
        <li>Wait 60 seconds for the rate limit window to reset</li>
        <li>Reduce concurrent Azure SDK calls during initialization</li>
        <li>Cache tokens in your application (Azure SDKs do this by default)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-3 text-neutral-900 dark:text-neutral-100">Token works on host but fails in container</h3>
      <p class="text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        Ensure the container has <code class="px-2 py-1 bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 rounded">local.credentials: azd</code> set in <code class="px-2 py-1 bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 rounded">azure.yaml</code>, and that <code class="px-2 py-1 bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 rounded">azd app run</code> (not <code class="px-2 py-1 bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 rounded">docker compose up</code>) was used to start the services. The credential forwarding setup only happens through <code class="px-2 py-1 bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 rounded">azd app run</code>.
      </p>
    </section>

